//! The USC programs the backend binds itself (not application shaders).
//!
//! `PVR_USC_FBLOAD` (and its float render-target variants `_F16X4`, `_F16`,
//! `_F32`) / `PVR_USC_FBLOAD_VS` are GENERATED by `yakogl-tools usc-blob`
//! (`tools/glsl2usc.sh`) from `tools/shaders/internal/fbload.{frag,vert}`:
//! do not edit them by hand. Every generated blob has the same three items so
//! the tool can emit them mechanically:
//!
//! ```text
//! pub const X_TEMPS: u32
//! pub const X_DWORDS: usize
//! pub static X: [u32; X_DWORDS]
//! ```
//!
//! `PVR_USC_CLEAR_FS_*` / `PVR_USC_CLEAR_FS2_*` are Mesa's clear-attach
//! programs as the driver's `pvr_usc_clear_fs_blob.h` /
//! `pvr_usc_clear_fs2_blob.h` carry them, copied here by hand;
//! `tools/pco_shc/gen_usc_blobs.py render --check` (a tools/check.sh row)
//! holds these words, and `PVR_USC_CLEAR_FS3_WORDS`, to the captures in
//! `tools/pco_shc/usc_blobs.txt`.

